  "summary": "One frozen, typed matrix for Aureline's M5 debug truth — debug sessions, attach targets, breakpoint specs, frame mappings, variable/watch snapshots, evaluate requests, console emissions, chronology capabilities, replay sessions, and notebook-debug parity records — across the core debugger, notebook debug, profiler, incident review, support export, AI context, review workspace, CLI/headless, and docs/help surfaces, with each object mapped to the proof packet that keeps it current. Debug truth stays explicit and replay-safe: launch, attach, core-file, replay, and inspect-only sessions stay distinct; breakpoint and mapping states stay visible; variables and watches never masquerade as live when stale; evaluation discloses side-effect risk; notebook, debugger, and replay share one support vocabulary; and a restored layout never implies reacquired authority over a target.",
